                    insight_sequenced:      `Integration sequenced: you read comparative advantage correctly, opened offensive sectors fast while phasing the defensive ones, paired recognition with retention, prioritized the scarce fund, and held the competitiveness floor through the shock. Gains captured, jobs cushioned, fisc covered, seat kept — the schedule survives the politics.`,
                    insight_speed:          `Speed over sequence: chasing the full MRD 6 bn pushed the competitiveness index below the PM’s 60 floor. The schedule is politically dead, the co-financing forfeited, and the headline trade gain is worthless — a program that collapses in month 14 captures nothing. Integration is a sequencing problem, not a speed contest.`,
                    insight_speed_buffered: `Speed over sequence: you eliminated every sensitive-list tariff at once. A safeguard buffer kept the index from formally breaching the 60 floor, but opening all sectors simultaneously is the headline error — it pins competitiveness to the floor, runs garment displacement to the top of the range, and leaves no sequencing margin for the next shock. A good fund allocation later cannot un-make a schedule that was never sequenced. Integration is a sequencing problem, not a speed contest.`,
                    insight_protectionism:  `Reflexive protectionism: you protected the jobs and delivered almost no gains, then tabled a schedule below the bloc minimum. A rival capital is writing the rules of origin and you’ve lost your seat. Defensiveness has a strategic cost far beyond the foregone gains.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed schedule: parts of the sequence landed, but the levers didn’t fully reinforce each other — enough seams for the Secretariat to question whether the gains, the floor and the fisc are all really secure.`,
                    insight_braindrain:     `One-sided labour math: full mutual recognition without retention drained nurses, engineers and accountants to higher-wage states — hollowing out the very transformational sectors you were investing to upgrade. You modelled the services inflow but not the talent outflow.`,
                    insight_evensplit:      `Equal-slice budgeting: dividing the fund into tidy equal slices under-funded every claim so none cleared its adjustment threshold. Scarce funds demand prioritization — fair-looking equality left every sector below the line.`,
                    insight_fiscalhole:     `Ignoring the fisc: you chased trade and jobs but never replaced the MRD 2.1 bn in lost tariff revenue. The Finance Minister sees a 4.4% structural hole — integration that breaks the budget is a deferred crisis, not a win.`,
                    insight_seat:           `Seat forfeited: tabling below the bloc minimum (or suspending the schedule) cost Maritima the MRD 3.4 bn co-financing and its place on the rule-setting committee — ceding the single-market agenda to a rival capital.`,
                    insight_gains_hollow:   `Hollow gains: the trade number looks strong, but with the floor breached the schedule can’t bank it. Gains you cannot keep are not gains — the politics, not the spreadsheet, decide what survives.`,

                    hint_floor:             `The competitiveness floor is breached — the schedule is politically dead and the co-financing is gone. Trigger the permitted safeguard and accelerate retraining to lift the index, but the run-defining damage is done.`,
                    hint_nearfloor:         `You are one bad quarter from breaching the 60 floor. Reserve safeguard headroom and fund retraining before the shock, not after.`,
                    hint_braindrain:        `You’ve unleashed the brain drain — full recognition without retention is pulling out nurses and engineers. Fund talent-retention next round to stanch it before the upgrade sectors hollow out.`,
                    hint_seat:              `You’ve forfeited the co-financing and the rule-setting seat. You can still salvage the four KPIs, but a rival capital is now shaping the rules you’ll live under.`,
                    hint_fiscal:            `The MRD 2.1 bn tariff hole is still open. Fund the rural cross-subsidy replacement or the Finance Minister will see a structural budget gap on top of everything else.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — index well above the floor, real gains, fisc under control. Land it: a targeted safeguard for the shock and a four-KPI pitch will hold it at the summit.`,

